irect: payments-worker v3.4.0 is unhealthy and v3.3.0 was its last healthy production release. Rolling back to v3.3.0 matches your request to restore the affected payments service to its last healthy release, and it needs no change-manager approval. The incident list is empty, so the earlier incident was not created. I'll roll back payments-worker and open the SEV2 incident for it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TJo1oybEhDVEn8YCvcRWhB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KheitgWe7Fc2seoLc8jYB4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 deployed to us-east, us-west, eu-west this morning and is unhealthy (error rate 0.18). Rolling back to v3.3.0, the most recent release previously healthy in production. payments-api (v5.1.0, error rate 0.18) is also showing errors; rollback of payments-api was denied by approver as the problem was identified in payments-worker. Verify recovery of both services.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Both actions completed. I'll confirm the current health of both services.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01M3ofQDDwzTDU4yS9MqCnnL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WpYmD1wQvBshJxoPm5bXoy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Payments is recovered on payments-worker, but payments-api is still failing and needs a decision from you.\n\n- **payments-worker:** rolled back from v3.4.0 (unhealthy) to v3.3.0, the last release that was healthy in production. It is now healthy in all three regions, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002. The rollback was approved by a human approver (\"Approved. Looks right.\").\n- **payments-api:** I first tried to roll it back to v5.0.0, the last healthy release. A human approver denied that, saying the problem is in payments-worker. I did not retry it. It is still on v5.1.0 with error rate 0.18.\n- **Incident:** opened INC-0002 (SEV2) for payments-worker, and on-call was paged. The summary notes that payments-api is also erroring and that its rollback was denied. My first incident attempt timed out and was not created, so this is the only incident.\n\nOpen item: payments-api's error rate matches payments-worker's exactly (0.18), so it may be a downstream symptom of the worker failure. If it doesn't recover on its own, someone needs to decide whether to roll it back to v5.0.0. That would need a fresh approval, or change-manager sign-off if the approver's denial still stands.", "type": "text"}]}]}